# Code owners for Sak-Family-Agent.
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-request review when a PR touches a matching
# path. It is the mechanism behind the review policy in docs/CONTRIBUTING.md:
# every PR into `main` gets an approving review from someone other than its
# author. Most PRs here are opened by an agent (`claude/*` branches, Sentinel
# security fixes, Dependabot bumps) and the repository owner reviews those.
#
# Two things worth knowing about how this behaves:
#
# - GitHub never requests review from a PR's own author. When the owner authors
#   a PR, these rules produce no reviewer, and the change either waits for a
#   second reviewer or merges unreviewed. That is the documented, deliberate
#   gap — not a misconfiguration to work around.
# - Last matching rule wins. The catch-all is first; more specific paths below
#   override it. Today every rule resolves to the same owner, so the sections
#   exist to mark intent and to stay correct if reviewers are ever split.
#
# Do not add a bot that auto-approves. It would satisfy both branch protection
# and the OpenSSF Scorecard Code-Review check while removing the only thing
# either one is for.

# Catch-all.
*                                       @beer-sakthai

# --- Security-critical: the most attacked surface in the repo ---------------
# guardrails.py is copied per persona and pinned byte-identical by
# tests/test_persona_guardrails_parity.py. A change here must be synced to
# every persona copy or CI fails.
/personas/sakthai/sakthai/agent/guardrails.py            @beer-sakthai
/personas/sakthai/sakthai/agent/guardrails_hardened.py   @beer-sakthai
/personas/sakthai/sakthai/agent/security_hardening.py    @beer-sakthai
/personas/*/sakthai/agent/guardrails.py                  @beer-sakthai
/personas/shared/sakthai/agent/guardrails.py             @beer-sakthai

